 \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f9e6f676f4cbc18433faa2a5d41207f11ad8f0b8cfcd107152da7d55e0fa5c1b","event_uuid":"32e7fd75-1778-4a63-af0b-3a3c9ac1fd7f","position":{"commit_sha":"4727bb45f6cb5066b70fd93a50e33899365c47be","position":"1787029897453035001-32e7fd75-1778-4a63-af0b-3a3c9ac1fd7f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e2fc6bf71cf7d6ce5b04c6340064244c9dd002eeebd32d917c5ce49a33429a3c","event_uuid":"327e40bb-cbe6-4f80-a1a0-67b2516f8fba","position":{"commit_sha":"a048648e08cd5bcab1c9fa73478591a76587610a","position":"1787029900500212001-327e40bb-cbe6-4f80-a1a0-67b2516f8fba"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":"","claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 classification (2026-08-17): the reported mechanism is CONFIRMED, but the not-a-bug guard classifies the requested behavior as `feature-request` / current `intended-behavior`, so Phase 2 is locked pending an explicit contract change. Runtime reproduction with `[reconciler] rich_text_cutover = \"clould\"` showed `rebar config validate` exit 0 with `OK — no removed inputs are set`, while `rebar config` rejected the value as outside `[both, cloud, dc, off]`. Source tracing confirms `_validate` at `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py:112-142` intentionally calls only `scan_tombstones`; it does not call typed resolution. Authoritative contract: `docs/config.md:577-585` explicitly defines this command as a non-raising sweep of every tombstoned input, non-zero iff an error-class tombstone is present; the command docstring/help and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py:217-228` encode the same behavior. Git blame/history shows implementation, docs, and tests were introduced together in commit 3eb3e71337, ruling out an accidental regression. Recommended non-fix disposition absent a product decision: close/reclassify as not-a-bug. If the user explicitly approves broadening the command contract, treat that as a feature-scope decision and define the aggregation semantics before RED/GREEN implementation.","timestamp":1787017801850497001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Scope authorization (2026-08-17): the user explicitly approved changing the command contract for this bug. In scope: aggregate validation of live typed configuration values, including enum and non-enum coercion failures, while preserving the same-run tombstone report. This authorization supersedes the prior not-a-bug pause and unlocks Phase 2 once the updated file-impact plan has a fresh signed review. Reliability constraint: do not claim validation coverage for config classes that cannot be deterministically enumerated through the real layering/coercion path.","timestamp":1787017994888387001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Repair verification report\n\nProblem: `rebar config validate` reported tombstones but did not validate known typed values.\n\nProven root cause: `_validate` only called `scan_tombstones`; the canonical `_SECTIONS` coercers were reached only through fail-fast config loading. The real CLI added a second mechanism: pre-dispatch store mounting called `tracker_dir_override()` and raised on `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR` before validation could aggregate anything.\n\nProof: the held-out real-CLI subprocess combined a tombstoned env input with invalid `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` and `mcp.http_port`. It was RED before repair, and temporary traceback instrumentation localized the early exit to `_main_dispatch -> ensure_store_mounted_best_effort -> tracker_dir_override`. Instrumentation was removed.\n\nTest: `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py::test_config_validate_aggregates_tombstones_and_typed_errors` was held out from the fixer. It is GREEN after repair. Removing the `config validate` no-auto-mount guard reintroduced the exact defect and returned the oracle to RED; the guard was restored. Refactoring litmus passes because the oracle asserts only CLI exit/output.\n\nFix: validation now drives the canonical per-key coercers across user/project/env/CLI layers, aggregates every ConfigError alongside tombstones, preserves unknown/reserved-section policy, and skips store mounting only for `config validate`. Documentation/help describe the expanded contract.\n\nScope and safety: no new dependency; no existing test weakened. Normal `config`, list, and other commands retain auto-mount behavior. Focused config/contracts: 89 passed. `make lint` and `make typecheck` passed.\n\nSiblings/parity: construct coverage is centralized through `_SECTIONS`, so enum, integer, boolean, and other registered coercers share the rule across all four layers. CLI is the validation surface; ordinary library loading intentionally remains fail-fast, and there is no MCP/API validation operation requiring parity.\n\nReplication: the original mixed tombstone + typed-invalid scenario now exits 1 and reports all three diagnostics in one invocation. Residual risk: malformed TOML remains governed by the pre-existing non-aggregation behavior and was not changed in this typed-value bug.","timestamp":1787022114787145001}],"created_at":1787005332044942001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fd4b401a-3252-4396-aa46-030e77ebbde7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"52bf-bc40-3fcb-4729"},{"link_uuid":"557c91c2-05e8-4eb4-893a-6d6f39b512f6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"},{"link_uuid":"7808983f-c172-4199-ae73-5bc6148e6121","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b8a0-1733-1333-4e44"}],"description":"## Problem\n`rebar config validate` reports success for invalid typed configuration values because it scans only removed/tombstoned inputs from raw TOML and deliberately bypasses the coercing `load_config()` path. The command name and success message imply that the project configuration was validated, so operators can receive a false green result for malformed enum values.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. In `rebar.toml`, set `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = \"clould\"` (an invalid enum value).\n2. Run `rebar config validate`.\n3. Observe exit 0 / `OK — no removed inputs are set.`\n4. Run `rebar config` and observe that the typed loader correctly rejects the invalid value.\n\n## Expected\n`rebar config validate` should validate the full supported configuration surface, including typed coercion and enum constraints, while still reporting all tombstoned inputs in one run. It should exit non-zero and identify invalid values such as `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = \"clould\"`.\n\n## Actual\nThe command only calls the tombstone scan over raw TOML, so invalid enum values and potentially other malformed live keys pass.\n\n## Evidence\n- `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py::_validate` only calls `scan_tombstones`.\n- `_raw_toml_tables` explicitly bypasses the coercing/raising `load_config` path.\n- `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` enforces `rich_text_cutover` via `_as_choice(..., {\"off\", \"cloud\", \"dc\", \"both\"})`, but that path is not reached by `config validate`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar config validate` returns non-zero for invalid values on live typed keys and reports each invalid key with an actionable diagnostic.\n- [x] Tombstone aggregation behavior remains intact; a single run reports removed inputs and typed-value errors rather than aborting after the first issue.\n- [x] Tests cover an invalid `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` value and at least one non-enum typed-value failure.\n- [x] Documentation accurately defines the command as full config validation.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py","reason":"aggregate tombstone and typed-config diagnostics in config validate"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"route config validate through the aggregated typed-validation command path"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py","reason":"cover enum, non-enum, and combined tombstone diagnostics through the real CLI"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document the full typed-validation contract"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"],["relates_to","b8a0-1733-1333-4e44"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"32e7fd75-1778-4a63-af0b-3a3c9ac1fd7f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["config","validation","bug"],"ticket_id":"acf9-154e-ca76-4aac","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar config validate does not reject invalid typed config values","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["08c9908d-a4e7-460d-b1b2-9277e051079b","2b18646e-f0e2-412c-afc6-56945ecbddf1","4c6a37c9-994c-473a-bbd5-bc2e39e6f645","1e5739f2-5dfb-40c7-927f-a1a917e3d04a","53e9fe20-d86c-45a5-8f3d-26a7a8a7ac2c","cd7ac538-249b-4fa9-9c13-a87f4a454d55","e6fd9fd4-4788-4b39-bf3d-5bdd81a84e0a","557c91c2-05e8-4eb4-893a-6d6f39b512f6","a77de12e-fbb4-48eb-a3d1-b6fb878f8a95","7808983f-c172-4199-ae73-5bc6148e6121","779a3435-50d9-4c87-832c-69cac94c9906","4df1d6e5-822b-4f65-b2a7-7ed9aff62fcc","32e7fd75-1778-4a63-af0b-3a3c9ac1fd7f","327e40bb-cbe6-4f80-a1a0-67b2516f8fba"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787033230415061741,"uuid":"bde5ed9f-e3b2-4423-b636-99e3e199a48d"}